{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T15:37:58Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-48770"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Conjecture Let $Diff^{r}(M)$ be the space of $C^{r}$ Diffeomorphisms on the connected, compact and boundaryles manifold M and $\\chi^{r}(M)$ the space of $C^{r}$ vector fields. There is a dense set $D\\subset Diff^{r}(M)$ ( $D\\subset \\chi^{r}(M)$ ) such that $\\forall f\\in D$ exhibit a finite number of attractor whose basins cover Lebesgue almost all ambient space $M$ This is a very Deep and Hard problem in Dynamical Systems. It present the dream of the dynamicist mathematicians."}, "statement_sha256": "50469f6e60adaecf459e2458d03c6b50a3f01e62cad387d282705c03137e6700"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-48770"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha256": "18bd699ffebcd1d56ba4fc8083ec2329704311d3a34f31188b4f66257b01bb9b", "problem_id": "problem:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a", "root_obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a-root", "route_id": "route:um-opg-48770-jacob-palis-conjecture-finitude-of-att-14e4bf8a-source-fidelity", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "supersedes": null}
